cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its evidence, cite this versioned record."
title: "ARFTR: Anchor-Restored Factorized Temporal Residual"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Huseyinli
    given-names: Abdulla
repository-code: "https://github.com/abdullahuseyinli-dot/arftr"
url: "https://github.com/abdullahuseyinli-dot/arftr"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Person-centered activity classification using an actor-memory anchor,
  complementary posture and locomotion evidence, a motion-specific template
  residual, and a constrained same-track temporal update. ARFTR retains
  85.383648 percent macro-F1 on 4,977 adaptively reused Okutama development
  centers. Includes the original seven-arm component study, aggregate evidence,
  an experimental knowledge graph, and the preserved research lineage.
  This development result is not independent confirmation. Version 1.0.0
  identifies the separately named ARFTR project, not a new model evaluation.
keywords:
  - human activity recognition
  - transfer learning
  - DINOv2
  - ARFTR
  - actor memory
  - factorized residuals
  - Okutama-Action
  - domain adaptation
  - calibration
  - evaluation methodology
  - temporal modeling
  - motion identifiability
